{"ts":"2026-07-26T22:34:25.668Z","author":"harness:opencode","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"opencode","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-a5w7vv"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"As an operator, I can ask pm a question in plain prose and receive the exact structured query plus its bounded answer, so insight never requires memorizing the flag grammar"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Exploration story (spike + ADR only). Natural-language intent compilation: map a prose question ('what blocked the release last week', 'which items has this agent touched') onto the structured query surface (list/search/graph filters) with the compiled query always shown, deterministic, and inspectable. The compiled query is the product: NL is an input convenience, never a hidden second query engine. Acceptance of any implementation slice is measured by the retrieval quality contract (pm-p1g43q), not by prose plausibility. Horizon: far (4+), after the grammar freeze (pm-agou) so the compilation target is stable."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Story"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":4},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["adr-needed","agent-ux","exploration","horizon:far","nl-intent","search","spike"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-26T22:34:25.668Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T22:34:25.668Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:opencode"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ydp6"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ca24d971ddf4c9bd93070c3b738c3122f94e745461c3771a297ec080b3d35ac7","message":""}
